Setting up Android OS as a virtual machine in VMware Workstation for use as a victim machine in security testing or GitHub repository experimentation requires using an x86-compatible Android build such as Android-x86 or Bliss OS. Standard ARM-based Android images will not run on PC virtualization platforms like VMware without significant emulation overhead.  The key is to use a lightweight, x86-optimized Android distribution, allocate sufficient hardware resources (especially CPU and RAM), and configure boot parameters correctly to avoid graphical issues. 


